      "topic": {
        "text": "Logical operators in Java",
        "refs": ["Q0000", "Q0001"]
      },
      "explanation_text": {
        "text": "The AND operator (&&) combines two boolean expressions so that the result is true only when both expressions are true. The NOT operator (!) reverses the boolean value of an expression, turning true into false and vice‑versa.",
        "refs": ["Q0000", "Q0001"]
      },
      "explanation_type": null
    },
    {
      "topic": {
        "text": "If statements in Java",
        "refs": ["Q0002", "Q0003", "Q0004"]
      },
      "explanation_text": {
        "text": "An if statement evaluates a boolean expression inside parentheses; if the expression is true, the statement or block of code that follows is executed. Curly braces define a code block that is executed as a unit when the condition is true.",
        "refs": ["Q0003", "Q0004"]
      },
      "explanation_type": null
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "exemplifies": {
        "text": "Temperature‑based messaging",
        "refs": ["Q0003", "Q0004"]
      },
      "example_text": {
        "text": "If temperature > 30, print \"it's a hot day\" and \"drink plenty of water\"; else if temperature is between 20 and 30, print \"it's a nice day\"; otherwise print \"it's a cold day\".",
        "refs": ["Q0003", "Q0004"]
      },
      "example_type": null
    }
  ],
  "facts": [
    {
      "fact_text": {
        "text": "A boolean variable named \"has criminal record\" is initialized to false.",
        "refs": ["Q0000"]
      },
      "fact_type": null
    },
    {
      "fact_text": {
        "text": "Applying the NOT operator to a false boolean yields true.",
        "refs": ["Q0001"]
      },
      "fact_type": null
    },
    {
      "fact_text": {
        "text": "When both the first condition (high income or good credit) and the second condition (no criminal record) are true, the person is eligible for a loan.",
        "refs": ["Q0002"]
      },
      "fact_type": null
    },
    {
      "fact_text": {
        "text": "In the example, the variable temperature is set to 32.",
        "refs": ["Q0003"]
      },
      "fact_type": null
    },
    {
      "fact_text": {
        "text": "If the condition temperature > 30 is true, the code inside the following curly braces is executed.",
        "refs": ["Q0004"]
      },
